WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.741
Write Elixir get

00:00:01.576 --> 00:00:03.180
an FPGA circuit

00:00:03.702 --> 00:00:05.294
FPGA circuits are

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.437
usually written register

00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:07.204
by register in

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:08.949
Verilog or VHDL

00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:10.986
Elixir HLS generates

00:00:10.798 --> 00:00:11.953
that hardware from

00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:13.475
ordinary Elixir functions

00:00:13.286 --> 00:00:13.993
instead

00:00:14.518 --> 00:00:15.779
A function defined

00:00:15.591 --> 00:00:16.841
with defhls still

00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:17.301
runs on the

00:00:17.112 --> 00:00:17.937
CPU

00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:19.128
and also becomes

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:19.683
a circuit

00:00:19.822 --> 00:00:20.812
Each circuit is

00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:21.850
simulated against its

00:00:21.661 --> 00:00:22.958
Elixir function and

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.795
used only if

00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:24.821
the results match

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.763
Version 0.1.0 is an

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:28.801
early first release

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:30.110
that synthesizes integer

00:00:29.922 --> 00:00:30.652
functions

00:00:30.806 --> 00:00:31.773
with types like

00:00:31.584 --> 00:00:32.975
u32 setting the

00:00:32.787 --> 00:00:33.565
bit width

00:00:33.704 --> 00:00:34.624
It builds on

00:00:34.435 --> 00:00:36.216
CIRCT and Icarus

00:00:36.027 --> 00:00:36.852
Verilog

00:00:37.374 --> 00:00:38.388
Full story on

00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:39.095
the dashboard
